class.description:
Describes how a [TileMapPathGraph] turns the cells of a [TileMapLayer] into a pathfinding graph. As a [Resource] it can be saved and edited in the inspector.
Costs and blocked cells come from custom data layers of the [TileSet], given by name. Paint them in the TileSet editor: add a custom data layer of type [bool] (for example [code]"blocked"[/code]) and one of type [float] (for example [code]"cost"[/code]), then set the values per tile.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var options = TileMapPathGraphOptions.new()
options.neighbor_mode = TileMapPathGraphOptions.NEIGHBOR_MODE_SIDES_AND_CORNERS
options.blocked_data_layer = "blocked"
options.cost_data_layer = "cost"
var graph = TileMapPathGraph.create($Ground, options)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var options = new TileMapPathGraphOptions();
options.NeighborMode = TileMapPathGraphOptions.NeighborModeEnum.SidesAndCorners;
options.BlockedDataLayer = "blocked";
options.CostDataLayer = "cost";
var graph = TileMapPathGraph.Create(GetNode<TileMapLayer>("Ground"), options);
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
Changes take effect at the next [method TileMapPathGraph.update_all].
